    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.42,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.7,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings sit on a very flat plateau at about 1.34 from 7 h to 18 h, after growth that was still roughly doubling each hour (0.19, 0.42, 0.93, then 1.32). That abrupt flattening is what detector saturation would look like. I checked the 18 h aliquot at two dilutions. At 10x it read 0.1451, which scales to 1.45. At 40x it read 0.0349, which scales to 1.40. Both are above the undiluted 1.34, and they roughly agree with each other (about 1.40–1.45). The gap is small, about 4–8%, and I had only one read per dilution, so noise could explain part of it. The evidence points to mild undiluted-read compression, with true OD at 18 h of about 1.4 or a little higher. It is not conclusive."
  },
